      "math_academy_id": "q-12534",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given $P(A|B)=0.4$, $P(B)=\\frac{1}{2}P(A)$, find $P(B|A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the multiplication law, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cap B) & =P(B)\\cdot P(A|B) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}P(A)\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.2P(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(B|A),$ we use \n\n$$\nP(B|A)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known expressions into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(B|A) & =\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.2P(A)}{P(A)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.2\\cancel{P(A)}}{\\cancel{P(A)}} \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
